// Created     : 2026-09-30
//
// Description : The caption of a native check box on an FT panel, as a TextBox beside the box: readable in
//               the FT colours, and a click on it ticks the box.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use Windows.pkg

/* WHY A CHECK BOX NEEDS ONE. The FT panels give their native children the FT ground and ink
   (cFTModalPanel's FTColorChildren), and a TextBox draws its label in that ink. A CheckBox draws its own
   caption in the Windows theme's colour, whatever its TextColor says - dark text on the dark ground. So the
   check box gets no caption of its own, and this TextBox beside it carries it:

       Object oPadded_cb is a CheckBox
           Set Size to 10 10
           Set Location to 42 11
       End_Object

       Object oPadded_tb is a cFTCheckBoxCaption
           Set Location to 43 22
           Set Label to "Keep same width padded with spaces"
           Set phoCheckBox to (oPadded_cb(Self))
       End_Object

   A click on the caption does what a click on the box does: the box takes the focus, flips and counts as
   changed (Changed_State) - the way DataFlex's own AutoLabel hands a click on a form's label to the form. */
Class cFTCheckBoxCaption is a TextBox

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        // The check box this is the caption of.
        { DesignTime=False }
        Property Handle phoCheckBox 0
    End_Procedure

    Procedure Mouse_Down
        Handle hoBox
        Get phoCheckBox to hoBox
        If (hoBox = 0 or not(Enabled_State(hoBox))) Begin
            Forward Send Mouse_Down
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Send Activate of hoBox
        Set Checked_State of hoBox to (not(Checked_State(hoBox)))
        Set Changed_State of hoBox to True
    End_Procedure

    // A caption holds nothing to save. A dialog's Broadcast Recursive Request_Save must stop here rather than
    // pass up to a data-aware parent - a group or a panel - that would save its DD again.
    Procedure Request_Save
    End_Procedure

End_Class
